      "body": "## What\n\nReports the interactive client's turn state to the terminal with the [Program Status Protocol (OSC 7501)](https://www.superlogical.com/rex/docs/build/program-status), so agent dashboards and terminals that implement it show Hermes as `idle`, `working`, `blocked`, or `done`.\n\nConcretely: Herdr.app lists a terminal as an agent only when its program reports state this way. Pi and Claude Code do; Hermes does not, so a Hermes pane shows up as a plain terminal next to them.\n\n## Why the client\n\nThe agent runs in the local `hermes serve`/gateway process, which has no terminal: plugin hooks fire there, where `/dev/tty` does not exist and `HC_TERMINAL_SOCKET` is not set. The interactive client (`CLIChatTurnMixin`, plus `GatewayChatView` for the gateway-attached view) is the process that owns the tty and the only one that knows when a turn starts and ends, so the reports are emitted there.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `hermes_cli/program_status.py` (new): gated `report(state, kind=None)` writing `ESC ] 7501 ; state=…:app=hermes … ST` to `/dev/tty`, plus `idle()` / `working()` / `blocked()` / `done()` wrappers. Identical states are skipped; every error is swallowed.\n- `cli.py`: `idle()` when the interactive loop starts.\n- `hermes_cli/cli_chat_turn_mixin.py`: `working()` when the agent thread starts, `done()` when the turn settles.\n- `hermes_cli/cli_modal_mixin.py`: `blocked(\"permission\")` while a dangerous-command approval waits, `working()` once it is answered.\n- `hermes_cli/gateway_chat_view.py`: `idle()` at view start, `working()` on submit, `done()`/`idle()` on completion, `blocked()` on an approval or clarify request, `working()` once it settles.\n- `tests/hermes_cli/test_program_status.py`: gating, payload, dedupe, and failure swallowing.\n\n## Gating\n\nReports are sent only inside a Herdr pane — `HC_TERMINAL_SOCKET` (Herdr.app) or `HERDR_ENV=1` (Herdr TUI). `HERMES_PROGRAM_STATUS=0` turns them off, `=1` sends them on any terminal. Unknown OSCs are ignored by every other terminal, and the writes are zero-width, so the rendered output is unchanged.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `pytest tests/hermes_cli/test_program_status.py`\n- In a Herdr.app pane: start `hermes`, confirm the pane reports `idle`; send a prompt, confirm `working` then `done` (`hc ls` shows `agent: hermes, status: …`).\n- Verified locally on macOS against Herdr 0.1.13 (`hc`): `idle` at startup, `working` → `done` across a turn. The approval path is wired to the CLI's approval callback but was not exercised interactively.\n",
